# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
#
# Generated from: specs/241-wait-for-retained-active-workers-instead-of-exiting-execute/requirements.md
Feature: Wait for retained active workers instead of exiting execute
  The execute controller previously returned status 0 when it
  found a live s<N>-* worker that was not idle/done on the
  current step. This was fixed by waiting with the existing
  Herdr agentWait path, then validating the handoff, and by
  failing closed on a step-name mismatch.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A live issue worker is reused
    Given /sdlc-execute is running for explicit issue 42 or a resumed selected queue
    And a live agent matching s42-* already exists for that issue
    When the controller observes that worker
    Then it does not create a second worker for the same issue and step

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: An active retained worker does not end the command
    Given a retained worker such as s42-verify is working
    When the controller would previously print Existing worker …; no second worker started and return success
    Then /sdlc-execute does not return merely because the worker is active
    And it remains responsible for the selected issues

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Settlement wait does not busy-spin or shorten Herdr wait
    Given a retained matching worker is still running
    When the controller stays attached
    Then it waits with herdr agent wait and no timeout argument
    And it does not use a tight CPU-consuming poll loop
    And it detects idle or done after that wait

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: A passed non-intervention handoff advances automatically
    Given the retained matching worker settles
    And .omp/sdlc/handoffs/42-start.json validates as status passed and intervention false
    When the controller consumes the handoff
    Then it marks start complete and starts the next workflow step without a manual /sdlc-execute reinvoke

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: The queue continues through merge and close
    Given selected issues are still open
    When each step's passed non-intervention handoff is consumed
    Then the queue continues through delivery until each selected pull request is merged and each selected GitHub issue is closed

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Later selected issues stay serial
    Given issues 42 and 43 are selected
    When issue 42 is still not both merged and closed
    Then s43-start is not started
    And issue 43 starts only after issue 42 is merged and closed

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Failed blocked missing invalid stalled and intervention outcomes stay fail-closed
    Given a retained or new worker settles into a failed, blocked, missing, invalid, stalled, or intervention-required handoff, or wait itself fails
    When the controller evaluates that outcome
    Then it does not return success
    And the relevant worker pane stays open
    And run.json records issue, step, and reasonCode
    And stdout names the issue, step, worker, pane, and reason

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: Interrupted execute remains resumable
    Given the controller is interrupted after run state has been persisted
    When /sdlc-execute is invoked again with the same explicit issues or as a resume of that run
    Then it resumes from persisted run state
    And it does not recreate completed work or duplicate live workers

  @SCN009 @regression
  Scenario: Safety gates remain intact
    Given existing Herdr, git, and GitHub preflight rules
    When execute runs after this fix
    Then HERDR_ENV, socket, pane, OMP integration, gh auth, dirty-tree, spec-created, approval, and dependency gates still fail closed
    And the orchestrator pane still does not edit product code, implement tasks, open pull requests, stop Herdr, use --kind pi, or stash reset or discard user work

  # --- Edge Case ---

  @SCN010 @regression
  Scenario: Focused tests prove reuse wait continue and fail-closed
    Given the focused execute controller tests
    When they run
    Then they fail on the pre-fix status-0 live-worker return
    And they prove a live retained worker is reused, waited for, and continued after a valid passed non-intervention handoff
    And they keep fail-closed coverage for failed, blocked, missing, invalid, stalled, and intervention-required outcomes
